ROWS = [
('tense',1,'At the moment, the technicians ___ the new sensor.',['test','are testing','tested','have tested'],1,'at the moment 把观察点放在说话时正在进行的活动，复数主语用 are testing。','一般现在时通常描述习惯或事实，并不自动表示此刻正在进行。'),
('tense',1,'On weekdays, Maya usually ___ to the office.',['walk','is walking','walks','has walked'],2,'usually 与 on weekdays 给出习惯性背景，第三人称单数一般现在时加 -s。','不要把主语单数与动词原形混用；第三人称单数规则只作用于一般现在时的肯定句。'),
('tense',1,'We ___ the museum yesterday afternoon.',['visit','have visited','are visiting','visited'],3,'yesterday afternoon 是已经结束的过去时段，应使用一般过去时 visited。','现在完成时通常不与明确且已经结束的过去时间直接搭配。'),
('tense',2,'The road was wet when we left; it ___ all night before that.',['rains','had rained','has rained','will rain'],1,'叙述基点为过去的离开，降雨发生在更早的过去，用过去完成时 had rained 表示先后。','过去完成时需要过去参照点；不能因为动作发生很久以前就机械地使用。'),
('tense',2,'I ___ this password since I joined the team, and I still use it.',['use','used','have used','had used'],2,'since 引出起点，still use it 明确状态延续到现在，使用现在完成时 have used。','单独的一般过去时会倾向把使用看作已结束；since 后的从句仍可用过去时 joined。'),
('tense',2,'Look at the sky. It ___ snow; those clouds are very dark.',['is going to','has to','used to','had to'],0,'当前可见迹象支持将来预测，be going to 是合适结构。','used to 表示过去习惯；has to 是义务或基于条件的必然，不能在这里代替未来趋势结构。'),
('tense',2,'At eight last night, I ___ dinner when the lights went out.',['cooked','am cooking','was cooking','have cooked'],2,'过去某时正在发生的背景活动用过去进行时，突然发生的停电用一般过去时。','when 后出现过去时并不要求主句也必须一般过去时；要区分背景和事件。'),
('tense',3,'By the time you arrive tomorrow, we ___ the equipment.',['install','will have installed','had installed','are installed'],1,'by the time 引出未来截止点，安装将在该点之前完成，用将来完成时 will have installed。','时间从句里的 arrive 用现在形式表示将来，但主句仍需根据完成关系选择。'),
('tense',2,'I ___ the answer now. (know，用一般现在时填空)',['know'],None,'know 表示认知状态，此语境使用一般现在时。','状态动词通常不用于进行体，但在特定语义转换或修辞中可能有例外，不能说所有状态动词永远不可进行。'),
('tense',3,'The kitchen smells wonderful because Jo ___ bread for the last hour.',['bakes','has been baking','had baked','will bake'],1,'活动从一小时前延续到现在，且留下当前可感知结果，用现在完成进行时强调过程。','现在完成进行时不保证动作仍在继续；它也可描述刚结束而结果仍明显的活动。'),
('tense',2,'When the train ___ tomorrow, send me a message.',['will arrive','arrives','arrived','has arrived yesterday'],1,'when 引导将来时间状语从句时，通常用一般现在时表示将来。','这条规则不适用于所有含 when 的从句：间接疑问 I wonder when it will arrive 可以用 will。'),
('tense',3,'She ___ to call you, but the network failed before she could dial.',['has intended','had intended','will intend','is intended'],1,'had intended 表示过去本来打算做的事；后文给出未能实现的原因。','不要把 be intended to（被设计用于）与 intend to（打算）混淆。'),

('voice',1,'The laboratory ___ every evening by the cleaning team.',['cleans','is cleaned','is cleaning','has cleaning'],1,'主语 laboratory 是清洁动作的承受者；习惯性被动结构是 is cleaned。','被动语态需要 be 与过去分词，不能只加 -ing 或使用主动第三人称形式。'),
('voice',2,'Please use the side door. The main entrance ___ right now.',['repairs','has repaired','is being repaired','was repairing'],2,'right now 表示正在进行；入口承受维修动作，用现在进行时被动 is being repaired。','is repaired 是一般现在时被动或结果状态，不能准确表达正在施工这一过程。'),
('voice',2,'The missing files ___ before the audit began yesterday.',['had been recovered','have recovered','were recovering','will be recovered'],0,'恢复发生在过去的审计开始之前，且文件为受事，用 had been + 过去分词。','先判断时态先后，再判断主语是否执行动作；不能只看到 before 就忽略被动。'),
('voice',2,'The invitations must ___ before Friday.',['send','be sent','be sending','have send'],1,'情态动词后接动词原形，被动为 must be sent。','must 后不能直接接过去分词 sent；have send 也不是完成式，过去分词应为 sent。'),
('voice',3,'He was made ___ the report again.',['write','writing','to write','written'],2,'使役 make 在主动 make somebody do 中省略 to，转成被动 was made to do 时恢复 to。','不能把主动使役结构的省略规则原样照搬到被动句。'),
('voice',2,'This coat ___ soft. Choose the natural linking-verb form.',['feels','is felt','is feeling by','has felt by'],0,'这里 feel 作连系动词，描述主语性质，使用主动形式 feels + 形容词。','描述触感的连系结构并不是省略了 by 的被动；触摸某物的 feel 又可作实义动词。'),
('voice',3,'The plan is expected ___ next month.',['approve','to approve','to be approved','being approved'],2,'be expected 后接不定式，plan 又是 approve 的承受者，所以用 to be approved。','被期待与被批准是两个不同的语法层次，后一个不定式也需表现被动关系。'),
('voice',2,'Which sentence keeps the meaning of “Someone has stolen my bicycle”?',['My bicycle has stolen.','My bicycle has been stolen.','My bicycle was stealing.','My bicycle has being stolen.'],1,'现在完成时主动变被动后，时态信息保留为 has been，实义动词变过去分词 stolen。','has been stolen 不说明具体小偷，也不必补一个未知的 by somebody。'),
('voice',3,'The printer needs ___; the rollers are worn.',['to repair','repairing','repaired','be repaired'],1,'need + -ing 可以表达被动含义，needs repairing 等同于 needs to be repaired。','need 后接 to repair 时，主语通常执行修理动作；本句打印机是受修对象。'),
('voice',1,'The parcel ___ delivered yesterday. (be 的过去时，单数)',['was'],None,'单数 parcel 与一般过去时被动搭配 was delivered。','delivered 本身是过去分词，时态和主谓一致主要由 was 承担。'),
('voice',3,'“The documents were looked after carefully.” 中的 after 能否省略？',['能，变被动要删除介词','不能，look after 是本义所需的动词短语','能，只要保留 carefully','必须改成 by'],1,'look after 表示照看；介词 after 属于这个动词短语，转被动时仍应保留。','并非所有词后的小词都可删除，删除后会改变词义或破坏及物关系。'),
('voice',3,'Which verb normally cannot form a personal passive in “An accident ___ last night”?',['was caused','was reported','was witnessed','was happened'],3,'happen 在这里是不及物动词，通常不能写成 was happened；应为 An accident happened。','caused、reported、witnessed 可带宾语并有被动；是否可被动取决于相应义项的及物性。'),

('article',1,'She waited for ___ hour before the office opened.',['a','an','the a','不需要任何限定词'],1,'hour 的 h 不发音，开头是元音音素，因此使用 an。','a/an 根据发音而非书写的首字母判断。'),
('article',1,'They are building ___ university near the station.',['an','a','two','these'],1,'university 开头是辅音音素 /j/，单数可数名词初次泛指用 a。','元音字母 u 开头不等于元音音素开头。'),
('article',1,'I bought a notebook. ___ notebook has a green cover.',['A','An','The','Some'],2,'第二次提及同一本 notebook，听者已经能够识别，使用 the。','不是所有第二次出现的名词都机械地加 the；关键是语境是否指向可识别的同一对象。'),
('article',2,'In this general statement, choose the natural form: “___ patience is essential when teaching beginners.”',['A','An','The','不填冠词'],3,'patience 是不可数抽象名词，这里泛指一种品质，通常用零冠词。','若特指某次表现出的耐心，可以使用 the patience she showed。'),
('article',2,'Please give me ___ advice about the interview.',['an','a piece of','many','a few'],1,'advice 通常不可数，可以用 a piece of advice 表示一条建议。','a few 和 many 通常修饰复数可数名词；不能把 advice 直接写成 an advice。'),
('article',2,'There is ___ milk left, so we can still make two cups of tea.',['a little','few','a few','many'],0,'milk 不可数，a little 表示有少量，后文 can still make 体现肯定含义。','little 更强调几乎没有，a few 则搭配可数名词复数。'),
('article',2,'___ of the two passwords works, so I must reset the account.',['Neither','Both','Every','All'],0,'two 给出二者范围，neither 表示两者都不，且可接单数谓语 works。','either 表示两者中的任一，不是两者都失败。'),
('article',2,'There are six routes. You may choose ___ route; all are safe.',['either','neither','any','both'],2,'超过两个选项且没有限制，any 表示任何一个。','either 一般指两个中的任一个；不能在六条路线的普通语境中替代 any。'),
('article',2,'I need ___ ten minutes to finish.',['another','other','others','the others'],0,'another 可放在 数词 + 复数时间单位 前，another ten minutes 表示再要十分钟。','another 不总是只能直接修饰一个单数名词；它还可修饰整体数量短语。'),
('article',3,'He is ___ European researcher working on ___ honest review.',['an; a','a; an','a; a','an; an'],1,'European 以 /j/ 开头用 a，honest 的 h 不发音用 an。','必须分别判断两个名词短语的首音，不能只看 e 和 h。'),
('article',2,'The students arrived one by one. ___ student received a badge.',['Each','Both','All','Many'],0,'each 后接单数可数名词，逐个分配的语义与 one by one 一致。','all students 需要复数形式；both 只限定两个。'),
('article',3,'Which sentence is the clearest standard form?',['I have a good news.','The news is encouraging.','These news are encouraging.','I have many news.'],1,'news 在标准英语中通常作不可数名词，谓语用单数 is。','词尾 -s 不一定表示复数；需要表达多条新闻时可用 several pieces of news。'),

('agreement',1,'Neither of the two keys ___ the door.',['open','opens','opening','are opening'],1,'正式书面英语中 neither of + 复数名词 通常按单数处理，使用 opens。','口语中可能出现复数一致，但本题明确采用正式书面语规范。'),
('agreement',2,'The number of visitors ___ rising, but a number of tickets ___ still available.',['are; is','is; are','is; is','are; are'],1,'the number of 的中心词是 number，用单数；a number of 表示许多，搭配复数名词时谓语用复数。','不要因为两种结构都含 number 就使用相同的一致规则。'),
('agreement',2,'Each engineer and each designer ___ a separate login.',['have','has','are having','were having'],1,'由 each 修饰的并列单数成员作主语，通常按单数逐个理解，用 has。','并列有 and 不意味着在所有结构中都必须使用复数谓语。'),
('agreement',1,'Please send the file to Nina and ___. (I 的宾格)',['me'],None,'介词 to 后用宾格 me；并列另一人不改变代词格。','不能因 Nina and 听起来正式就选 I；删去 Nina and 后结构仍应成立。'),
('agreement',2,'The laptop on the desk is ___. (my 的名词性物主代词)',['mine'],None,'mine 独立作表语，表示 my laptop；其后不再接名词。','my 是限定词，必须修饰名词；mine 不是 my 的复数。'),
('agreement',2,'The manager, together with two assistants, ___ attending the meeting.',['are','is','were','have been'],1,'主语中心词是单数 manager，together with 插入短语不改变主语的数。','不要让距离谓语最近的 assistants 干扰一致判断。'),
('agreement',2,'Ten kilometres ___ too far for the small child to walk today.',['are','were','is','have been'],2,'距离作为一个整体量来评价时，谓语通常用单数 is。','不是所有带复数单位的量词短语都按普通复数个体处理。'),
('agreement',2,'The equipment ___ checked before use.',['need to be','needs to be','are to be','have to be'],1,'equipment 通常是不可数名词，单数一致用 needs to be checked。','不能根据中文“设备”可能有多台，就把 equipment 当成复数。'),
('agreement',3,'Everyone should bring ___ own notebook. Choose the inclusive modern standard pronoun.',['their','them','theirs','themselves'],0,'单数 they 的物主限定词 their 可以回指性别未指定的 everyone，是现代标准用法。','everyone 的谓语仍用单数；使用 their 不要求把 everyone 的谓语改为复数。'),
('agreement',2,'I repaired the chair ___. (myself / me 中选填)',['myself'],None,'myself 在这里表示独自亲自完成，可作强调性附加语。','反身代词不能无条件替代宾格；Please email me 不能随意改成 email myself。'),
('agreement',3,'One of the students who ___ selected has already replied.',['was','were','is','has been'],1,'关系代词 who 的先行词在通常解读下是复数 students，定语从句用 were selected；主句 one 用 has replied。','不要把主句的 one 的单数一致直接套用到修饰 students 的关系从句。'),
('agreement',2,'There ___ a notebook and two pens on the counter. Choose the standard nearest-noun agreement used in this exercise.',['is','are been','have','were be'],0,'存在句在此使用就近一致，第一个名词短语 a notebook 为单数，使用 is。','实际书面语可重组为 A notebook and two pens are... 以避免风格分歧；不可把此规则扩展为所有倒装句的通则。'),

('preposition',1,'The interview starts ___ 9:30 a.m.',['in','on','at','by with'],2,'具体钟点通常使用 at。','by 9:30 表示最迟不晚于该时刻，并不等于恰在该时刻开始。'),
('preposition',1,'The workshop will take place ___ Monday morning.',['at','in','on','to'],2,'特定某一天的上午用 on Monday morning。','泛指在上午是 in the morning，但加上具体星期后通常改为 on。'),
('preposition',2,'She has lived here ___ 2020.',['for','since','during','from of'],1,'2020 为起始时间点，持续至现在用 since。','for 后通常接持续时间段，例如 for six years。'),
('preposition',2,'Please submit the report ___ Friday, so it is available for Saturday’s review.',['by','during','since','for'],0,'by Friday 设定最迟截止日。','until Friday 表示某状态或活动持续到周五，不能普遍替代截止含义的 by。'),
('preposition',2,'We travelled to the island ___ ferry.',['by','on a by','with','in by'],0,'表示交通方式时可用 by + 零冠词交通工具，如 by ferry。','登上具体一艘船可说 on the ferry；交通方式与具体载具短语的结构不同。'),
('preposition',2,'The team is responsible ___ testing the emergency system.',['to','for','with','at'],1,'be responsible for + 名词或动名词 表示对某事负责。','responsible to somebody 表示向某人负责，介词随语义关系变化。'),
('preposition',2,'The final decision depends ___ the safety inspection.',['of','to','on','at'],2,'depend on 是固定动词搭配，后接决定因素。','不能按中文“取决于”直接映射成 of；搭配须按英语结构记忆。'),
('preposition',2,'He apologised ___ being late.',['for','to','with','of'],0,'apologise for + 原因；向某人道歉则是 apologise to somebody。','for 与 to 分别连接原因和接受道歉的人，二者不能简单互换。'),
('preposition',2,'I look forward to ___ from you.',['hear','hearing','heard','have heard'],1,'look forward to 中的 to 是介词，后接动名词 hearing。','不是所有 to 都是不定式标记；要根据整个搭配识别。'),
('preposition',3,'The technician prevented the battery ___ overheating.',['from','to','for','of'],0,'prevent somebody/something from doing 表示阻止某人或物做某事。','与 stop...from... 相似；不能接 prevent...to do 来表达相同结构。'),
('preposition',2,'The two solutions are different ___ each other. Choose a widely accepted neutral form.',['from','than to','as','for'],0,'different from 是广泛通用的比较搭配。','different to 在英式英语、different than 在美式英语中也可成立，不能宣称它们在所有语境中错误。'),
('preposition',3,'“Despite ___ tired, she finished the test.” Fill with the -ing form of be.',['being'],None,'despite 是介词，其后可接动名词 being tired。','despite 后不能直接接完整有限分句 she was tired；可改为 despite the fact that she was tired。'),

('nonfinite',1,'They decided ___ the meeting online.',['hold','holding','to hold','held'],2,'decide 常接 to 不定式作补足语。','不同动词对后续结构有不同选择；不能把 enjoy doing 的规则套到 decide。'),
('nonfinite',1,'I enjoy ___ small robots.',['build','building','to building','built'],1,'enjoy 后接动名词 building。','to build 在这里不是 enjoy 的标准补足结构。'),
('nonfinite',2,'Please remember ___ the window before you leave.',['close','closing','to close','closed'],2,'remember to do 表示记得去做尚未完成的事，before you leave 给出待执行任务。','remember doing 表示记得曾做过的事，时间方向不同。'),
('nonfinite',2,'I clearly remember ___ this form last week.',['signing','to sign','sign','be signed'],0,'remember doing 回忆已发生的行为，last week 确定为过去经历。','remember to sign 是记住要去签，不能表达已经签过的记忆。'),
('nonfinite',2,'After working for two hours, we stopped ___ some water.',['drink','drinking','to drink','drunk'],2,'stop to do 表示停下原先的活动，转而做另一件事。','stop drinking 表示停止喝水，和本句工作后喝水的意图相反。'),
('nonfinite',2,'The doctor told him to stop ___ because it was harming his health.',['smoke','to smoke','smoking','smoked'],2,'stop doing 表示停止某个活动；这里停止的是吸烟。','stop to smoke 表示停下别的事去吸烟，会逆转含义。'),
('nonfinite',2,'The instructor let us ___ the machine first.',['try','to try','trying','tried'],0,'let + 宾语 + 动词原形，主动使役结构不用 to。','let 的结构和 allow somebody to do 不同，不能互相套用。'),
('nonfinite',2,'The manager allowed us ___ early.',['leave','leaving','to leave','left'],2,'allow somebody to do 使用带 to 的不定式。','allow doing 无明确人物宾语时也可成立，如 allow smoking，但本句有 us。'),
('nonfinite',3,'___ from the hill, the village looks very small.',['Seeing','Seen','To see','Having seeing'],1,'被观察的是 village，它和 see 为被动关系，使用过去分词 Seen 作状语。','分词逻辑主语应与主句主语对应，Seeing 会使村庄成为观看者。'),
('nonfinite',3,'___ all the cables, the engineer switched on the device.',['Having checked','Having been checked','Checked','To have checking'],0,'检查先于开机完成，且 engineer 执行检查，用完成主动分词 Having checked。','Having been checked 会把工程师理解为被检查对象，与语境不符。'),
('nonfinite',3,'She was the first researcher ___ the unusual signal.',['detecting','to detect','detected','having detect'],1,'序数词修饰的人物名词后常用 to 不定式作后置修饰，the first...to detect。','不能因为动作已发生就把所有修饰都变为过去分词；detected 还会造成被动含义。'),
('nonfinite',3,'“The form is worth ___ carefully.” Fill in the -ing form of read.',['reading'],None,'be worth doing 中主动形式的 -ing 可表达值得被做，故用 reading。','不要写 worth to read 或机械套被动写 being read；标准搭配是 worth reading。'),

('clause',1,'The engineer ___ designed this bridge will speak today.',['who','which','where','when'],0,'先行词指人，关系从句缺主语，可用 who。','where 和 when 是关系副词，不能直接充当 designed 的主语。'),
('clause',2,'The book ___ I borrowed is on the table. Choose the option that can be omitted without changing the structure.',['which','whose','where','when'],0,'which 在限制性定语从句中作 borrowed 的宾语，可以省略。','关系代词作主语时通常不可直接省略，whose 还需修饰后面的名词。'),
('clause',2,'My aunt, ___ lives in Kyoto, is visiting next week.',['that','who','what','where'],1,'逗号标记非限制性关系从句，指人用 who，通常不用 that。','that 可用于不少限制性关系从句，但不可机械替代非限制性从句中的 who。'),
('clause',2,'This is the workshop ___ the old engine was restored.',['which','where','who','whose'],1,'从句 engine was restored 已有主语和谓语，缺的是地点状语，用 where。','地点先行词并不总用 where；若从句缺宾语则可用 which，如 the workshop I visited。'),
('clause',3,'The reason ___ she gave was convincing.',['why','which','where','when'],1,'gave 在此缺宾语，关系代词 which 连接先行词 reason 并作宾语。','看到 reason 不要固定选 why；why 连接的是表示原因状语的结构。'),
('clause',3,'I do not know ___ the replacement part will arrive.',['what','when','which that','whose that'],1,'间接疑问从句询问到达时间，用 when。','本句不是将来时间状语从句，will arrive 在间接疑问结构中正常。'),
('clause',2,'Could you tell me where ___?',['is the nearest exit','the nearest exit is','does the nearest exit be','the nearest exit does'],1,'嵌入式疑问从句使用陈述语序，主语 the nearest exit 在 is 前。','礼貌问句的主句已经疑问化，从句不再使用直接疑问倒装。'),
('clause',3,'___ surprised the team was the very low error rate.',['That','What','Which of','Because'],1,'What 在主语从句中既连接从句又作 surprised 的主语，表示让团队惊讶的事。','that 只起连接作用，不能补上从句内部缺失的主语。'),
('clause',3,'The proposal ___ the schedule should be changed was accepted.',['which','where','that','what'],2,'that 引导同位语内容从句，解释 proposal 的内容；从句内部成分完整。','此处不是用关系代词指代 proposal 作宾语，which 不能直接替换。'),
('clause',2,'Take a map ___ you get lost. The purpose is preparation, not a condition for taking it.',['in case','unless','even if only','as though'],0,'in case 表示为防可能出现的情况而预先采取措施。','if you get lost 容易表达迷路后才拿地图，与预先准备的意图不同。'),
('clause',3,'We cannot start ___ every participant has signed in.',['until','because of','despite','during'],0,'not...until 表示直到某时才开始，until 后可接完整从句。','during 是介词，后面通常接名词短语，不直接连接完整有限从句。'),
('clause',3,'___ the instructions were clear, several participants asked for help.',['Although','Because of','Despite','In spite of'],0,'although 是连接词，后可接 instructions were clear 这样的完整从句。','despite/in spite of 后接名词或动名词，不能直接接本题的完整从句。'),

('conditional',1,'If you heat ice sufficiently, it ___.',['melts','melted','would melt','had melted'],0,'描述一般规律可使用零条件句：if + 一般现在时，主句一般现在时。','条件句不都表示假想未来，要区分一般规律与具体事件。'),
('conditional',2,'If the weather improves tomorrow, we ___ outside.',['will practise','would practise','had practised','practised'],0,'真实可能的未来条件，if 从句用现在时，主句可用 will + 动词原形。','不要仅因为 tomorrow 就在普通条件状语从句中写 will improve。'),
('conditional',2,'If I ___ more free time now, I would join the course.',['have','had','had had','will have'],1,'与当前事实相反或较不现实的假设，if 从句用过去形式 had，主句 would join。','这里的过去形式表达假设距离，不是简单叙述过去时间。'),
('conditional',3,'If they had checked the address, they ___ the wrong building yesterday.',['would not visit','will not have visited','would not have visited','do not visit'],2,'对过去未发生的条件及结果作反事实推想，结果用 would have + 过去分词。','would not visit 通常对应现在或将来假想，不能清楚表达过去结果的反事实。'),
('conditional',3,'If she had taken the earlier flight, she ___ here now.',['would be','would have been yesterday','will be','had been'],0,'条件指过去未采取的行动，结果指现在状态，是混合条件句，结果用 would be。','不能只看 if had done 就固定让主句也用 would have done；需要判断结果时间。'),
('conditional',3,'I wish I ___ the answer right now.',['know','knew','had known yesterday','will know'],1,'wish 后对当前情况的不满足通常用过去形式 knew。','had known 表示对过去不知道的遗憾；时间参照不同。'),
('conditional',3,'I wish I ___ that careless email yesterday.',['did not send','had not sent','would not send yesterday','do not send'],1,'对已经发送的过去邮件表示后悔，用 wish + 过去完成时 had not sent。','wish 后的过去完成时表达与过去事实相反，而不是普通的过去叙事。'),
('conditional',3,'If I ___ you, I would ask for written confirmation. Choose the formal hypothetical form.',['were','am','will be','had been yesterday'],0,'正式假设建议中常用 If I were you，were 是非真实条件形式。','口语可能出现 was，但本题明确要求正式假设形式；不能把 am 当作此反事实结构。'),
('conditional',3,'Unless the weather ___, the match will continue. (change，用一般现在时)',['changes'],None,'unless 表示 if...not；将来条件从句一般用现在时，单数 weather 配 changes。','unless 本身含否定条件义，通常不再加 not 来重复否定。'),
('conditional',4,'Had I seen the warning, I ___ the process.',['would stop','would have stopped','will have stopped','had stopping'],1,'Had I seen 是 If I had seen 的省略 if 倒装，结果为过去反事实 would have stopped。','句首 had 不能被误解为普通疑问；上下文仍是一整个条件复句。'),
('conditional',3,'It is time we ___ the old policy.',['review','reviewed','will review','have reviewing'],1,'It is time + 主语 + 过去形式 表示现在早该做某事，常用 reviewed。','过去形式在此不代表动作已发生，也可以改写为 It is time to review...。'),
('conditional',4,'The panel recommends that each candidate ___ interviewed separately.',['is','was','be','has been'],2,'表示建议的 that 从句可用原形虚拟式；被动用 be interviewed。','英式英语还可用 should be interviewed，但当前选项中只有 be 符合该结构。'),

('modal',1,'You ___ wear a seat belt; it is a legal requirement.',['must','might','may','would'],0,'must 表示强制义务，符合明示的法律要求。','might/may 通常表示可能或允许，并不能表达必须履行的义务。'),
('modal',2,'You ___ bring lunch tomorrow; food will be provided.',['must not','do not have to','cannot','should not have'],1,'do not have to 表示没有必要，学校将供餐。','must not 表示禁止，不能把没有必要误读为不允许。'),
('modal',2,'The room is completely dark and nobody answers. They ___ be at home. Choose the strongest negative deduction.',['must not','cannot','do not have to','need not'],1,'cannot be 表示基于证据作强烈否定推断。','must not 常表示禁止；表达“不可能在家”的标准教学对应通常是 cannot be。'),
('modal',3,'The key is in your hand, so you ___ have left it at the office.',['cannot','must','should','need'],0,'cannot have + 过去分词 对过去作强烈否定推断；手上有钥匙与落在办公室矛盾。','cannot 后直接接 left 不构成所需完成式，要保留 have。'),
('modal',3,'You ___ have backed up the file. Now the only copy is lost.',['should','may','can','need not'],0,'should have done 在此表示过去本应做而未做，语境给出损失结果。','should do 是现在或未来建议，不能完整表达对未做过往行为的评价。'),
('modal',3,'I bought extra tickets, but my friend had already bought enough. I ___ have bought them.',['need not','must not','could not','shall not'],0,'need not have done 表示确实做了，但事后看来没有必要。','did not need to do 只说明没有必要，本身不保证实际做了；语用重点不同。'),
('modal',2,'___ I borrow your charger for ten minutes? Choose a polite request for permission.',['May','Must','Need','Ought'],0,'May I...? 是请求许可的常见礼貌结构。','Must I...? 问是否必须，不能表达借用请求；ought 后通常还需 to。'),
('modal',3,'After several failed attempts, we ___ open the locked box yesterday. Choose the form that clearly reports one successful achievement.',['were able to','could generally','can','may'],0,'过去某次具体成功做到某事，用 were able to 清楚表达实现结果。','could 常表示过去一般能力；肯定叙述特定成功时 were able to 更明确，感官等动词语境有例外。'),
('modal',2,'When she was six, she ___ read simple stories without help.',['can','could','may','must have'],1,'过去持续存在的一般能力用 could。','must have 后需过去分词，并表示过去推断，不是普通过去能力。'),
('modal',3,'You had better ___ the instructions before starting.',['read','to read','reading','have reading'],0,'had better 后接不带 to 的动词原形。','had better 不是一般过去时；它通常针对当前或未来提出较强建议。'),
('modal',2,'The replacement part might ___ tomorrow. (arrive 的正确形式)',['arrive'],None,'情态动词 might 后接动词原形 arrive。','不要按单数主语给 arrive 加 -s；情态动词后的形式不受这种第三人称变化支配。'),
('modal',4,'“He must have been working.” 中 must have been working 主要表达什么？',['对过去持续活动的强推断','过去的法定义务','未来的禁止','现在完成时的一般习惯'],0,'must 表推断，have been working 是完成进行形式，把推断指向过去或此前延续的活动。','义务 must 与推断 must 要通过上下文和补足形式识别，不能只背 must=必须。'),

('comparison',1,'This route is ___ than the motorway.',['short','shorter','shortest','most short'],1,'than 引出比较对象，short 的比较级为 shorter。','最高级通常用于一个范围中的极值，而不是普通的两项比较。'),
('comparison',2,'Of the three plans, this is ___.',['more practical','the most practical','practical than','as practical'],1,'of the three 给出比较范围，practical 的最高级为 the most practical。','多音节形容词一般不用 practicalest；比较级与最高级的范围不同。'),
('comparison',2,'The second task is not as difficult ___ the first.',['than','as','that','like than'],1,'同级比较结构为 as...as，否定时 not as...as 表示不如。','不能把比较级的 than 放进 as...as 结构。'),
('comparison',2,'She speaks English more ___ than I do.',['fluent','fluently','fluency','fluentest'],1,'修饰动词 speaks 需副词 fluently，比较级为 more fluently。','fluent 修饰名词或作表语；fluency 是名词，均不能直接在此修饰 speaks。'),
('comparison',2,'The new device is much ___ than the old one.',['efficient','more efficient','most efficient','as efficient'],1,'much 可加强比较级 more efficient，表示高效得多。','不能写 much efficient 来替代 very efficient，也不能把 much 自动看作最高级标志。'),
('comparison',3,'The ___ you practise, the ___ the task becomes.',['more; easier','most; easiest','much; easy','more; easy'],0,'the + 比较级...，the + 比较级... 表示越……越……。','两个分句都需要比较结构，不是前面有 more 后面就能用原级 easy。'),
('comparison',2,'The instructions were ___ clear that nobody asked a question.',['such','so','too','enough'],1,'so + 形容词 + that 从句；clear 为形容词。','such 通常修饰名词短语，如 such clear instructions that...。'),
('comparison',2,'This box is light enough ___ by one person.',['carry','to be carried','carrying','carried'],1,'形容词 + enough + to 不定式；box 为搬运受事，使用 to be carried。','enough 在形容词后，但在名词前，如 enough time；还需同时判断主动被动。'),
('comparison',3,'Which sentence clearly means the task was not difficult for me?',['The task was too easy for me to do.','The task was easy for me to do.','The task was so easily.','The task was enough easily to do.'],1,'easy for me to do 表示这项任务对我容易；主动不定式可修饰前面的受事名词。','too...to 通常表示程度过高而妨碍行动，不宜用来简单表达不困难。'),
('comparison',3,'The ___ news made everyone feel ___.',['surprised; surprising','surprising; surprised','surprised; surprised','surprise; surprisingly'],1,'surprising 描述消息让人惊讶的性质，surprised 描述人的感受。','-ing/-ed 的选择取决于语义角色，不是机械地规定物永远 -ing、人永远 -ed。'),
('comparison',2,'He worked ___ to meet the deadline. (hard / hardly 中选填)',['hard'],None,'hard 作副词表示努力地；hardly 表示几乎不。','不是所有副词都由形容词加 -ly 形成；词形相近时可能词义完全不同。'),
('comparison',3,'Choose the standard order: “a ___ desk”.',['wooden small round','small round wooden','round wooden small','wooden round small'],1,'多个定语形容词的常见顺序为大小、形状、材质，因此 small round wooden。','自然语序受强调和语境影响，但无特殊强调的中性名词短语通常按此顺序。'),

('structure',2,'Only after the inspection ___ the machine.',['we restarted','did we restart','we did restarted','restarted we did'],1,'only + 状语 位于句首，主句常用部分倒装：did + 主语 + 动词原形。','过去时由 did 承担，restart 不能再写成 restarted。'),
('structure',3,'Never before ___ such a complex failure.',['I have seen','have I seen','I did seen','have seen I'],1,'否定意义状语 never before 前置触发助动词与主语倒装，have I seen。','倒装不是把整个谓语放在主语前，过去分词 seen 仍留在主语后。'),
('structure',3,'Not until midnight ___ the final test.',['we finished','did we finish','had we finish','we did finish'],1,'not until 状语放句首，主句倒装，用 did we finish。','若写 We did not finish until midnight 则不需要这种前置倒装。'),
('structure',3,'Hardly had we sat down ___ the alarm rang.',['than','when','that','while than'],1,'hardly...when... 是常见时间关联结构，表示刚……就……。','no sooner 常与 than 搭配，两组结构不要交叉混用。'),
('structure',3,'No sooner had the meeting begun ___ the power failed.',['when','than','then','that'],1,'no sooner...than...；前置 no sooner 后主句 had the meeting begun 倒装。','than 在此不是普通形容词比较，而是整个关联结构的一部分。'),
('structure',2,'It was the backup cable ___ solved the problem.',['that','where','what','when'],0,'It was...that... 是强调句，突出 backup cable。','强调句去掉 It was 和 that 后应能还原 The backup cable solved the problem。'),
('structure',3,'Which sentence emphasises the time rather than the person?',['It was Lina who called at noon.','It was at noon that Lina called.','Lina, who called, was at noon.','Who was it Lina called noon?'],1,'It was at noon that... 把时间状语 at noon 放进强调位置。','强调时间时通常用 that，不是把强调结构误换成 where 或 when。'),
('structure',2,'“I have finished.” “So ___ I.”',['have','do','am','did'],0,'So + 对应助动词 + 主语 表示另一人同样如此，原句现在完成时用 have。','不能把所有附和句都写成 so do I，须匹配助动词和时态。'),
('structure',2,'“I cannot attend.” “Neither ___ I.”',['do','can','am','have'],1,'否定附和结构为 neither + 助动词/情态动词 + 主语，本句用 can。','Neither I can 不符合此附和倒装语序；Neither can I 本身已是否定。'),
('structure',3,'Seldom ___ this shortcut in production. (we / use，用一般现在时倒装填完整短语)',['do we use'],None,'seldom 含否定频率义，句首时使用 do we use 的部分倒装。','不要写 seldom we use；第三人称复数 we 对应助动词 do 而非 does。'),
('structure',3,'Only the team leader ___ the administrator password.',['knows','does know he','does he know','know'],0,'only 修饰主语 team leader 时不触发倒装，直接用单数谓语 knows。','only 在句首并非一律倒装，要看它修饰主语还是状语。'),
('structure',3,'Not only ___ the error, but she also explained its cause.',['she found','did she find','she did found','found she did'],1,'not only 引导的前置否定关联分句用部分倒装 did she find。','but also 所在后分句通常不因前一个分句倒装而再倒装。'),

('worduse',1,'Please ___ me the truth.',['say','tell','speak','talk'],1,'tell somebody something 可以直接接人和信息，tell me the truth。','say 通常不能直接写 say me the truth，应为 say...to me。'),
('worduse',2,'Could I ___ your umbrella until tomorrow? I will return it then.',['lend','borrow','owe','rent out'],1,'borrow 表示从别人处借入，return it then 说明说话人是借入者。','lend 表示借出，方向相反；rent out 通常表示出租。'),
('worduse',2,'The project will ___ several hours to complete.',['spend','take','costing','pay'],1,'物或任务作主语，表示耗费时间常用 take；take several hours to complete。','人 spend time doing，而不是把项目作主语写 spend several hours。'),
('worduse',2,'She ___ two hours checking the wiring yesterday.',['took','spent','cost','paid'],1,'人 + spend + 时间 + doing 是标准结构，过去时为 spent。','take 的常见句型为 It took her two hours to check...，结构不同。'),
('worduse',2,'The price has ___ sharply this month.',['risen','raised','arisen up','rose'],0,'rise 为不及物动词，价格自行上涨，完成时用过去分词 risen。','raise 通常及物，需施动者和被提高的对象；rose 是过去式而非过去分词。'),
('worduse',2,'The company plans to ___ prices next month.',['rise','raise','arise','rose'],1,'公司执行提高价格的动作，raise 直接接宾语 prices。','rise prices 不能表达这个及物关系；arise 通常表示出现或产生。'),
('worduse',2,'We missed the bus. ___, we arrived late.',['However','Therefore','Nevertheless','Although'],1,'前句给出原因，后句给出结果，因此 Therefore 合适。','however/nevertheless 表转折，although 是从属连接词，不能在此单独作句际结果连接。'),
('worduse',3,'The instructions were short; ___, they covered every safety step.',['nevertheless','because','therefore of','despite'],0,'nevertheless 连接前后出乎意料的对比：虽短仍全面。','despite 是介词，不可单独带逗号充当此处的句际连接副词。'),
('worduse',3,'Choose the sentence with a correct comma and conjunction relationship.',['The test failed, we investigated.','The test failed, so we investigated.','The test failed, because of we investigated.','The test failed so, we investigated.'],1,'两个独立分句可用逗号加并列连词 so 表示因果。','只用逗号连接两个独立分句是 comma splice；because of 后应接名词短语。'),
('worduse',3,'She speaks ___ English ___ Japanese, so she can help in either language.',['neither; nor','both; and','either; nor','not; but no'],1,'both...and... 表示两种语言都会，符合 either language 中任一种都能帮助的语境。','neither...nor... 表示两者都不，会与后文能力描述冲突。'),
('worduse',3,'The software is ___ reliable ___ easy to maintain. Both qualities are being added.',['not only; but also','either; nor','neither; also','although; and'],0,'not only...but also... 并列相同语法层级的形容词短语，表示两种优点。','并列应尽量保持结构平行；不能把不配套的连接词拼接在一起。'),
('worduse',3,'Choose the standard form: “She suggested ___ a second test.”',['we to run','running','to running','run to'],1,'suggest 可接动名词 running，或接 that we (should) run；不能使用 suggest somebody to do 的普通建议义结构。','suggest 与 advise 的补足结构不同，advise somebody to do 可以成立。'),
]

assert len(ROWS) == 144, len(ROWS)
